WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.840
Rollerball, the action-packed pinball game with the distinctly American touch.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:30.540
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.500
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:33.880
I'm Joe.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.140
And I'm Joe, is what I normally say.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:37.900
Yeah, I was like, whoa, hold on a minute.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.100
It's been a couple weeks, I forgot.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.940
Last episode, I think we said you were out trying to find Sam.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.020
No luck there? I found him.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.640
And I'm working on getting him back.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:49.960
Great. Oh, okay.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:53.040
Good update. I thought you found him, but you just decided to leave him.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.440
No, I found him, but for, you know, I don't want to spook him.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:57.960
So I'm not telling anyone where he is.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.580
I'm just, I'm the only one who knows where he is right now, and I will keep working on

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:02.740
him and maybe I'll convince him.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.940
Okay. I like that.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:10.660
It's the game with the distinctly American touch, but I just have to note right off the

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:13.920
bat that there are zero American game designers.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:17.320
This is Hall Labs with Satoru Iwata.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.260
This is weird, right?

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.060
Obviously, the American touch is referring to like the Statue of Liberty and the big apple

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.720
that's on the main menu screen and shit like that.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:32.240
But it feels weird that it has an American touch without any Americans working on it.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:37.780
Well, I'm just glad to see like some representation of American culture in an NES game.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:48.980
Like it mostly is just stuff from like pre-industrial Japan and some German influences, but you never really

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:51.540
get to see, you know, the big U.S.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:53.600
in video games.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:55.940
Yeah. Finally a game for Americans.

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:58.240
It's a good point though, Sean.

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:01.100
Where is the Genghis Khan pinball game?

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:05.480
Where is the Nobunaga pinball game?

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:06.980
True, true.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:12.560
But why have more of those when you've already gone to that well so often?

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:17.800
You have to, you have a fresh well of American culture right in front of you.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:22.200
You know what well they don't go to that often in NES video games?

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:23.280
What's that?

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:26.960
Pinball. Why all of a sudden is pinball back?

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:31.720
It's back-to-back games of pinball after years of no pinball.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:36.240
Maybe that's something they just like notice, like, hey, we haven't gone to this well too

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.220
often, only like twice now.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:46.560
Um, so let's, let's try again, but, but make it like, if you had to make a pinball machine,

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:48.500
but just put it on a cartridge.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:54.540
Uh, pinball, the launch game, the very first one that was years ago now, um, that was also

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.180
made by HAL Laboratories.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:57.660
They, they don't want you to know that.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:00.360
They want you to think Nintendo made all those black box games.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:07.000
It's not true. Uh, so with that in mind, I think last time we had a pinball game, it was trying, it was

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.320
trying to not be pinball.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:11.920
It had all these other modes that were like, you know, there was a ball and there were flippers,

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:15.480
