00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:59.680
So, I mean, this is, I'm a guy who does not play almost any actual pinball in his life.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:05.440
But why is this, uh, twice the length that a pinball machine could actually be?

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:07.200
Like, why couldn't a pinball machine be this length?

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:10.400
Is there technical limitations to the size?

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:17.460
Yeah, there, there's actually a, uh, physics, like a physics equation, um, that tells you that

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:20.540
it tells you how long a pinball machine can actually be.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:22.860
